description:
Private turn out paddock with stall, indoor stalls. Queen sized bed in a private bedroom in home. Kennel outside with a dog house 
for up to 3 dogs. Can accommodate RV/horse trailer but there are no septic hook ups. Extended stays & camping options are now available & owners often ride in the mountains. Come joins us!!” “Spring/summer stay option available, 
trainer available - build client list or bring your clients. Location notes: Southeast of Colorado Springs.

Fully fenced camping pad with electric and water and a separately fenced, attached turn out area for grazing and stretching their legs! There is room behind the parking area to unload your horses. We have a fully fenced RV 
site with an additional fenced yard attached for furry friends or extra space to hang out. The RV site is a concrete pad with full electric (50 amp) and water services. We are located on 15 acres with beautiful views of the stars at night; 
while still having the convenience of being 10 minutes from town for groceries or a quick run to pick up dinner or snacks! Location notes: We are just 10 minutes from Highway 44 and very close to Route 66.

Horse motel and vacation care for horses on the go! Spacious stalls with attached outdoor runs, large pasture areas, RV/camper water and electrical hookups as well as 
free WiFi. The Paard Yard is an excellent choice for a stay before or after the Canadian border crossings or enroute to the Montana wilderness. Breathtaking location, friendly people and 
superior horse care. Quick access off the highway. Close to small hotels, food, grocery, Missouri River world-class fishing sites, recreation areas and horse trails. Location notes: Cascade, Montana;

Overnight and short term boarding. Trail ride through the country side for free. Tons of wildlife and beautiful views of the Big Horn Mountains. 8 large turnouts with grass; 4 - 10' x 40' half covered runs; 
2 - large corrals; 7 - indoor stalls; outdoor riding area; electrical hook-ups only. Must have Coggins and health papers. Reserve by 4 p.m. Location notes: Exit 20 off I-90 1.6 miles north on WY 338 toward Decker, Montana. At fancy entrance, turn left (west) and drive straight up the lane to the barn. Coming from Billings, Exit 16 at Port of Entry off I-90, 
head east on Highway 338 1.1 miles. Cross the railroad tracks, turn right on Highway 338, drive 1.6 miles, turn right, drive straight up the lane to the barn.
